skill: "ledger-reconciliation"
sections[3]:
  - "# ledger-reconciliation\n\nReconcile sub-ledgers to the general ledger and resolve invoice discrepancies with recorded evidence. Use at each close, when a sub-ledger total disagrees with its GL control account, or when a customer or vendor disputes amounts. Produces journal proposals for the controller - it never posts directly.\n\nOwner: role-accounts-manager (pod-gna, finance). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"sub-ledger exports (AR, AP, billing); GL control account balances at close; source documents (invoices, credit notes, payment confirmations)\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/finance/ledger-recon.toon with matched[], delta analysis, discrepancy-log.toon with classifications; journal_proposals[] for controller review\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Export each sub-ledger and its GL control balance as of the same close date; a date mismatch stops the run before any matching starts.\n2. Match documents by document id first, then by counterparty plus amount window; matched items with zero delta need no further work.\n3. Compute the unexplained delta per sub-ledger with run_command and carry it in both directions (sub-ledger over GL, GL over sub-ledger) - direction matters for classification.\n4. Classify every delta item: missing document, timing (period edge), duplicate, currency rounding or data-entry error; an item with no classification stays unresolved and blocks sign-off.\n5. For customer and vendor disputes, assemble the evidence pack: the invoice, the payment confirmation, the exchange-rate record and the correspondence reference.\n6. Propose the correcting journal per resolved item with debit and credit lines explicit; the proposal is recorded, not posted - posting authority is the controller's.\n7. Emit ask_question to role-corporate-controller with journal_proposals[] and unresolved items; record the response per item.\n8. Write ledger-recon.toon and discrepancy-log.toon; carry unresolved items forward with their age so next close starts from facts, not memory.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\njournal proposals to role-corporate-controller; evidence packs to disputing counterparties.\n"
